        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "Bruker";
        skos:definition        "A global manufacturer of high-performance scientific instruments and analytical solutions for molecular and materials research, industrial analysis, and clinical applications. Their technologies include mass spectrometry, Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR), Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR), Raman spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction, and micro-CT imaging systems. It was founded in 1960 in Karlsruhe, Germany, and is now headquartered in Massachusetts, USA."@en;
