        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "CAMECA";
        skos:definition        "A company founded in 1929 in France, CAMECA is a company specialising in the provision of scientific instrumentation, particularly for mechanics, optics, and electronics. Specifically, CAMECA pioneered Electron Probe MicroAnalysis (EPMA) in the 1950s and Secondary Ion Mass Spectrometry (SIMS) in the 1960s. CAMECA is headquartered in Gennevilliers, France, and is a business unit of AMETEK Inc following its acquisition from the Carlyle Group in 2007."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L35::MAN0339";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
