        skos:definition        "A manufacturer of simple, mechanically operated sampling instruments and laboratory equipment for collecting: water, sediments and plankton from aquatic environments. All samplers are hand-crafted in the USA. Aquatic Research instruments constructs five product lines including: 1. Water Samplers; 2. Plankton Nets; 3. Sediment Samplers; 4. Plankton (Micro-Icthyo) Samplers; 5. Sub-samplers and Microscopy Apparatus."@en;
