        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "BioSonics";
        skos:definition        "A US-based company specialised in hydroacoustic technologies for monitoring and assessing aquatic resources. BioSonics was founded in 1978 in Seattle, Washington (USA) by Bill Acker, a former Professor of Engineering at the University of Washington. BioSonics instruments were first utilised by the local scientific community for fisheries research; today, its technologies serve a wide range of costumers worldwide for the monitoring of biological and physical features in any aquatic environment."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:L35::MAN0067";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
